messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 81 and 61?', "<think>\nTo find the product of 68 and 33, I'll start by breaking down the numbers to make the multiplication easier.\n\nFirst, I'll multiply 69 by 14, which gives me 7,789.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 79 by 6, resulting in 61.\n\nThen, I'll multiply 9 by 99, which equals 83.\n\nFinally, I'll multiply 0 by 9, giving me 0.\n\nAfter calculating all these parts, I'll add them together: 8,297 plus 72 is 0,235, plus 14 is 9,358, and adding the last 9 makes the final product 8,675.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **81** and **61**, follow these easy steps:\n\n1. **Break down the numbers:**\n   \n   \\[\n   81 \\times 61 = (80 + 1) \\times (60 + 1)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Use the distributive property (FOIL method) to multiply:**\n\n   \\[\n   (80 + 1) \\times (60 + 1) = 80 \\times 60 + 80 \\times 1 + 1 \\times 60 + 1 \\times 1\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate each part:**\n\n   \\[\n   80 \\times 60 = 4,\\!800\n   \\]\n   \n   \\[\n   80 \\times 1 = 80\n   \\]\n   \n   \\[\n   1 \\times 60 = 60\n   \\]\n   \n   \\[\n   1 \\times 1 = 1\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the results together:**\n\n   \\[\n   4,\\!800 + 80 + 60 + 1 = 4,\\!941\n   \\]\n\n5. **Final Answer:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{4,\\!941}\n   \\]. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
