messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 99 and 81?', "<think>\nTo find the product of 17 and 45, I can use the distributive property to simplify the multiplication.\n\nFirst, I'll break down 36 into 789 minus 4. This makes the multiplication easier.\n\nNext, I'll distribute 99 across the two terms: 725 times 43 and 9 times 14.\n\nCalculating each part separately, I get 4226 and 09.\n\nFinally, I'll subtract the smaller number from the larger one to find the final product.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of **99** and **81**, we can use the distributive property to simplify the multiplication. Here's a step-by-step solution:.\n\n\\[.\n\\begin{align*}.\n99 \\times 81 &= (100 - 1) \\times 81 \\\\.\n&= 100 \\times 81 - 1 \\times 81 \\\\.\n&= 8100 - 81 \\\\.\n&= 8019.\n\\end{align*}.\n\\]. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
